<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Isted</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">24–25 July <a href="/years/1850">1850</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Battle of Idstedt · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-schleswig-war">First Schleswig War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Isted, or Idstedt, was fought on 24–25 July 1850 near the town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schleswig">Schleswig</a> and was the largest battle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-schleswig-war">First Schleswig War</a>. The Danish army defeated the army of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schleswig-holstein">Schleswig-Holstein</a> provisional government, which fought alone after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> made peace with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a>. The victory restored Danish control of Schleswig, confirmed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> Protocol of 1852.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-isted.jpg" alt="Battle of Isted" width="320" height="183" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Niels Simonsen · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Niels_Simonsen_-_Slaget_ved_Isted_den_25._juli_1850_-_KMS847_-_Statens_Museum_for_Kunst.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
